<newsitem itemid="531466" id="root" date="1997-04-23" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Adcock lifts first half shr and div.</title>
<headline>Adcock lifts first half shr and div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Mar 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)  54.3	   vs 47.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		15.0	   vs 12.6</p>
<p>    Attrib income	  156.41	 vs 138.32</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   231.68	vs 203.40</p>
<p>    Tax			 74.14	 vs 63.92</p>
<p>    Operating income	206.99	vs 184.57</p>
<p>    Interest received     11.92	 vs 6.67</p>
<p>    Turnover		  958.31	vs 920.60</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  0.10 loss   vs 0.10 gain</p>
<p>Div payable July 1</p>
<p>on register May 9</p>
<p>Full name: Adcock Ingram Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Results are not directly comparable due to the merger with Premier Pharmaceuticals last May. As a result, the figures above have been presented on a pro forma basis which assumes that the merger had been effective from October 1, 1995.</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters had predicted EPS of 55.0 cents, with the range 53.6-56.5, and a dividend of 14.3, with range 13-15. -- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
